WEBVTT

00:00:10.582 --> 00:00:11.583
[dragon snorting]

00:00:11.666 --> 00:00:12.667
[gasps]

00:00:16.754 --> 00:00:19.757
This is where you've been for 20 years?

00:00:22.969 --> 00:00:24.804
You've been rescuing them.

00:00:28.391 --> 00:00:29.475
Unbelievable.

00:00:29.642 --> 00:00:31.144
You're not upset?

00:00:31.311 --> 00:00:33.563
What? No. [stammering] I don't know.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.857
It's a bit much to
get my head around, to be frank.

00:00:36.065 --> 00:00:37.609
It's not every day you find out

00:00:37.775 --> 00:00:40.904
your mother is some kind of crazy, feral,

00:00:40.987 --> 00:00:42.822
vigilante dragon lady.

00:00:42.906 --> 00:00:44.449
Oh. [chuckles]

00:00:46.659 --> 00:00:50.246
At least I'm not boring, right?

00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:55.084
I suppose there is
that one specific thing.

00:00:55.209 --> 00:00:57.253
Do you like it?

00:00:58.129 --> 00:00:59.589
[stuttering]

00:00:59.672 --> 00:01:01.299
I don't have the words.

00:01:04.427 --> 00:01:05.845
[sniffing]

00:01:06.387 --> 00:01:07.931
[Valka laughs]

00:01:10.475 --> 00:01:11.851
Can I…

00:01:12.435 --> 00:01:14.187
Oh, he's beautiful.

00:01:16.022 --> 00:01:18.107
[giggling]

00:01:18.191 --> 00:01:19.859
Incredible!

00:01:21.027 --> 00:01:24.030
He might very well
be the last of his kind.

00:01:24.197 --> 00:01:26.824
And look, he's your age.

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.117
Wow.

00:01:28.201 --> 00:01:30.036
No wonder you get along so well.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:31.829
[speaking gibberish]

00:01:33.122 --> 00:01:36.167
[gasps] And retractable teeth!

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.628
How did you manage to…

00:01:38.711 --> 00:01:40.171
I found him in the woods.

00:01:40.338 --> 00:01:43.466
He was shot down and wounded.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.558
This Snafflefang lost his leg
to one of Drago Bludvist's iron traps.

00:01:52.976 --> 00:01:56.062
This Raincutter
had her wing sliced by razor netting.

00:01:56.521 --> 00:01:59.065
And this poor Hobblegrunt

00:01:59.232 --> 00:02:01.693
was blinded by a tree snare

00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:04.904
and then left to die alone and scared.

00:02:05.822 --> 00:02:06.864
And what of this?

00:02:07.365 --> 00:02:09.909
Did Drago or his trappers do this, too?

00:02:09.993 --> 00:02:12.412
[Hiccup chuckles nervously] Oh, yeah…

00:02:13.997 --> 00:02:16.082
The crazy thing is…

00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:20.795
I'm actually the one who shot him down.

00:02:21.087 --> 00:02:23.006
Hey, it's okay, though.

00:02:23.172 --> 00:02:24.257
He got me back!

00:02:24.424 --> 00:02:25.717
Right, bud?

00:02:25.842 --> 00:02:27.593
You couldn't save all of me, could you?

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.262
You just had to make it even.

00:02:29.429 --> 00:02:32.140
So, peg leg!

00:02:33.182 --> 00:02:34.517
[laughs]

00:02:38.062 --> 00:02:41.065
What did your father think
of your Night Fury friend?

00:02:41.274 --> 00:02:43.526
He didn't take it all that well.

00:02:44.277 --> 00:02:47.363
But then he changed.

00:02:47.447 --> 00:02:48.698
They all did.

00:02:48.781 --> 00:02:51.868
Pretty soon, everyone back
home had dragons of their own.

00:02:53.244 --> 00:02:55.288
-If only it were possible.
-No, really.

00:02:55.413 --> 00:02:57.623
Believe me, I tried, as well,

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.793
but people are not
capable of change, Hiccup.

00:03:01.294 --> 00:03:05.339
Some of us were just born different.

00:03:05.423 --> 00:03:06.924
[dragons screeching]

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.885
[people shouting]

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:11.304
[man] Hoist the torches!

00:03:12.597 --> 00:03:15.767
[Valka] Berk was a land of
"kill-or-be-killed,"

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:18.519
but I believed peace was possible.

00:03:18.728 --> 00:03:19.854
[Stoick yelling]

00:03:19.937 --> 00:03:22.648
Stop! You'll only make it worse!

00:03:23.691 --> 00:03:26.277
[Valka] It was a very unpopular opinion.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.445
[Stoick yelling]

00:03:27.528 --> 00:03:28.613
[gasps] Hiccup!

00:03:29.322 --> 00:03:33.284
[Valka] Then, one night,
a dragon broke into our house,

00:03:33.451 --> 00:03:34.577
finding you in the cradle.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:35.828
[gasps]

00:03:37.038 --> 00:03:39.123
I rushed to protect you.

00:03:39.207 --> 00:03:41.042
[baby Hiccup giggling]

00:03:43.836 --> 00:03:45.463
But what I saw

00:03:45.588 --> 00:03:47.924
was proof of everything I believed.

00:03:54.806 --> 00:03:56.182
[crying]

00:03:57.475 --> 00:03:58.893
[gasping]

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.523
This wasn't a vicious beast,

00:04:03.648 --> 00:04:06.567
but an intelligent, gentle creature,

00:04:07.151 --> 00:04:08.361
whose soul

00:04:08.528 --> 00:04:10.196
reflected my own.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:11.989
-[Stoick grunts]
-[Valka gasps]

00:04:12.323 --> 00:04:13.366
[Stoick] Valka, run!

00:04:13.533 --> 00:04:15.701
[Valka] No! Don't!

00:04:20.039 --> 00:04:21.040
Hold on!

00:04:21.124 --> 00:04:22.208
[grunts]

00:04:23.543 --> 00:04:25.002
[Valka] No! Stoick!

00:04:25.128 --> 00:04:26.587
[Stoick] Valka!

00:04:28.381 --> 00:04:30.007
[Valka] Stoick!

00:04:32.009 --> 00:04:33.219
Valka.

00:04:35.012 --> 00:04:38.432
[Valka] You and your father
nearly died that night,

00:04:38.516 --> 00:04:41.477
all because I couldn't kill a dragon.

00:04:42.395 --> 00:04:44.730
It runs in the family.

00:04:44.897 --> 00:04:47.316
It broke my heart to stay away,

00:04:47.525 --> 00:04:50.361
but I believed you would
be safer if I did.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.406
How did you survive?

00:04:53.531 --> 00:04:56.492
Oh, Cloudjumper never meant to harm me.

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:59.871
He must have thought I belonged here.

00:05:00.538 --> 00:05:04.709
In the home of the great Bewilderbeast.

00:05:04.917 --> 00:05:07.086
The alpha species.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:10.298
One of the very few that still exist.

00:05:12.717 --> 00:05:14.552
Every nest has its queen,

00:05:14.719 --> 00:05:18.639
but this is the king of all dragons.

00:05:18.764 --> 00:05:23.186
With his icy breath,
this graceful giant built our nest.

00:05:23.603 --> 00:05:26.439
A safe haven for dragons everywhere.

00:05:27.315 --> 00:05:29.442
Wait, that's the ice-spitter?

00:05:29.609 --> 00:05:31.777
He's responsible for all that destruction?

00:05:31.944 --> 00:05:33.779
He protects us.

00:05:34.238 --> 00:05:37.992
We all live under his care
and his command.

00:05:38.075 --> 00:05:40.077
[young dragons chittering]

00:05:40.995 --> 00:05:43.372
[Valka] All but the babies, of course,

00:05:45.917 --> 00:05:47.501
who listen to no one!

00:05:47.627 --> 00:05:49.253
[Valka laughing]

